A Description of the Resources and Expected Deliverables of Assignment A0
=========================================================================


A. Resources
------------

This directory contains the following :

 1. This file (A0-README).

 2. A subdirectory called reference-implementations. It contains A0-sclp
    which is a reference implementation of the full compiler for language 
    Level  5. You can observe the AST, TAC, RTL, ASM for your input programs 
    by giving appropriate command line switches.(Use --help option)

 3. A subdirectory called example-programs. It contains the following
    subdirectories

    - Level-5-test-cases. This subdirectory contains some valid programs
      for level 5 of the language.

    - Level-5-invalid-test-cases. This subdirectory contains some invalid 
      programs for level 5 of the language.
    
B. Expected Deliverables
-------------------------

You are required to generate AST, TAC, RTL, ASM files for testcases using 
the reference implementation by giving appropriate command line switches,
and submit them as per the below format.

You need to submit a tarred gzipped version of your directory (file name
must be <groupid>.tar.gz) containing these generated files. On untarring, 
it must  produce the directory `groupid'  (e.g. `group1',  `group19').
Any deviation from this will be treated as non-submission.

